        },
        {
          "post_id": "476315",
          "text": "<p>The output $Y$ of a $2$ -bit comparator is logic $1$ whenever the $2$ -bit input $A$ is greater than the $2$ -bit input $B$ . The number of combinations for which the output is logic $1$ , is</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$4$</li><li>$6$</li><li>$8$</li><li>$10$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Digital Logic",
          "day": "Day 43"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "476311",
          "text": "Consider the Boolean expression:<br>\n<br>\n$$<br>\nf(A, B, C)=A B C+A^{\\prime} B^{\\prime} C+A^{\\prime} B C+A B C^{\\prime}+A^{\\prime} B^{\\prime} C^{\\prime}<br>\n$$<br>\n<br>\nWhat is the total number of literals in the minimum Sum of Products (SOP) form of the function?",
